Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.84,0:05:00.44,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,400,3240,3600)\pos(996.889,412.533)}Dāngyáng \NBridge
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.53,0:05:04.69,Default,Zhao Yun,0,0,0,,Yide, aid us!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.00,0:05:09.56,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(985.489,486.044)}Zhāng Fēi\NStyled: Yìdé
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.21,0:05:07.62,Default,Zhang Fei,0,0,0,,Zilong, hurry!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:07.62,0:05:09.20,Default,Zhang Fei,0,0,0,,I will stop the pursuers!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:39.68,0:05:43.28,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,400,3240,3600)\pos(335.839,419.555)}Madam Gān
Dialogue: 0,0:06:01.88,0:06:02.84,Default,People,0,0,0,,General Zilong!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:02.92,0:06:04.50,Default,All,0,0,0,,General Zilong has returned!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:04.50,0:06:05.19,Default,Zhao Yun,0,0,0,,My liege!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.84,0:06:06.86,Default,General,0,0,0,,General Zilong!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:06.86,0:06:07.50,Default,Jian Yong,0,0,0,,General Zhao!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.50,0:06:08.42,Default,Zhao Yun,0,0,0,,My liege!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.42,0:06:09.75,Default,Jian Yong,0,0,0,,General Zhao!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:09.75,0:06:10.92,Default,Zhao Yun,0,0,0,,My liege!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:10.92,0:06:12.25,Default,Jian Yong,0,0,0,,General Zhao!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.80,0:06:14.74,Default,Zhao Yun,0,0,0,,My liege!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.20,0:06:31.78,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,400,4300,4560)\pos(317.639,491.631)}Liú Bèi\N Styled: Xuándé
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.42,0:06:31.99,Default,Liu Bei,0,0,0,,Zilong!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:34.25,0:06:35.67,Default,Zhao Yun,0,0,0,,My liege!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.14,0:06:37.95,Default,Liu Bei,0,0,0,,Zilong!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:55.82,0:06:59.92,Default,Zhao Yun,0,0,0,,My crime can't be redeemed,\N even by ten thousand deaths.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.36,0:07:05.92,Default,Zhao Yun,0,0,0,,Lady Mi was crippled and refused to mount my horse.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:09.34,0:07:11.04,Default,Zhao Yun,0,0,0,,She threw herself down a well!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.60,0:07:18.12,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,400,2960,3520)\pos(883.823,402.755)}Mí Fāng
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.92,0:07:18.04,Default,Zhao Yun,0,0,0,,To bury her, I pushed down the wall!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:19.12,0:07:22.70,Default,Zhao Yun,0,0,0,,With your son by my bosom, I broke out of the siege!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:33.26,0:07:34.66,Default,Liu Bei,0,0,0,,Zilong, please rise...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:36.98,0:07:40.00,Default,Zhao Yun,0,0,0,,It was for your fortune that we were able to escape!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.82,0:07:43.44,Default,Zhao Yun,0,0,0,,Your son cried only a moment ago...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:45.38,0:07:47.90,Default,Zhao Yun,0,0,0,,but I don't feel any movement from him now...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.94,0:07:49.57,Default,Zhao Yun,0,0,0,,I failed to protect him!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:01.22,0:08:01.82,Default,Zhao Yun,0,0,0,,My liege!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:01.82,0:08:02.82,Default,Lady Gan,0,0,0,,My dear baby!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:03.00,0:08:05.54,Default,Zhao Yun,0,0,0,,Luckily, your son was unharmed.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.40,0:08:34.14,Default,Liu Bei,0,0,0,,Because of this baby,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:35.56,0:08:38.36,Default,Liu Bei,0,0,0,,I almost lost a great general!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:51.14,0:08:55.18,Default,Zhao Yun,0,0,0,,Even if my organs splatter onto the ground,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:55.18,0:08:58.32,Default,Zhao Yun,0,0,0,,I can never repay a fraction of your kindness!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:22.20,0:09:26.64,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,400,4000,4440)\pos(303.423,481.956)}Wén Pìn\NStyled: Zhòngyè
Dialogue: 0,0:10:22.16,0:10:26.16,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,400,3680,4000)\pos(311.768,488.335)}Cáo Rén\NStyled: Zǐxiào
Dialogue: 0,0:10:25.94,0:10:27.96,Default,Cao Ren,0,0,0,,This may be an ambush by Zhuge Liang.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:30.00,0:10:31.28,Default,Cao Ren,0,0,0,,Inform the Chancellor.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:31.28,0:10:31.72,Default,Soldier,0,0,0,,Yes!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.61,0:11:26.18,Default,Zhang Fei,0,0,0,,I am Zhang Yide of Yan!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:26.18,0:11:28.08,Default,Zhang Fei,0,0,0,,Who dares come fight me to the death!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:30.25,0:11:32.78,Default,Zhang Fei,0,0,0,,I am Zhang Yide of Yan!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:32.78,0:11:34.76,Default,Zhang Fei,0,0,0,,Who dares come fight me to the death!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:48.75,0:11:51.10,Default,Cao Cao,0,0,0,,Guan Yunchang once mentioned that:
Dialogue: 0,0:11:51.10,0:11:56.34,Default,Cao Cao,0,0,0,,"Zhang Yide can slice through \Na horde to behead the commander,"
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.34,0:11:58.24,Default,Cao Cao,0,0,0,,"like reaching into a pocket."
Dialogue: 0,0:11:59.81,0:12:01.34,Default,Cao Cao,0,0,0,,Now that we ran into him,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:01.34,0:12:02.96,Default,Cao Cao,0,0,0,,we must not underestimate him.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:08.16,0:12:10.18,Default,Zhang Fei,0,0,0,,Zhang Yide of Yan is right here!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:10.18,0:12:11.64,Default,Zhang Fei,0,0,0,,Who dares come fight me to the death?!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:49.92,0:12:50.66,Default,General,0,0,0,,Chancellor,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:50.66,0:12:52.44,Default,General,0,0,0,,there may be an ambush across the bridge.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:06.65,0:13:08.02,Default,Zhang Fei,0,0,0,,Fight or don't fight!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:08.02,0:13:09.78,Default,Zhang Fei,0,0,0,,Run or don't run!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:09.78,0:13:11.44,Default,Zhang Fei,0,0,0,,Which is it?!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:22.56,0:13:23.53,Default,Generals,0,0,0,,Retreat!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:50.12,0:13:54.66,Thinking,Narrator,0,0,0,,In the thirteenth year of the Jian'an era, 208 CE,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:54.66,0:13:57.48,Thinking,Narrator,0,0,0,,under overwhelming pressure from Cao Cao,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:57.48,0:14:01.72,Thinking,Narrator,0,0,0,,Liu Cong of Jing Province, son of\N Liu Biao, surrendered his cities to him.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:02.16,0:14:05.46,Thinking,Narrator,0,0,0,,Liu Bei abandoned Fancheng with\Nthe people and sailed the Yangtze river,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:05.46,0:14:07.34,Thinking,Narrator,0,0,0,,fleeing to Han Ford in defeat.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:02.92,0:14:06.96,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,400,3700,4040)\pos(1022.889,330.578)}Jiāngxià
Dialogue: 0,0:14:07.34,0:14:10.20,Thinking,Narrator,0,0,0,,He turned to Liu Qi for temporary refuge in Jiangxia.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:10.88,0:14:13.79,Thinking,Narrator,0,0,0,,The victorious Cao Cao gathered 830,000 \Ntroops at the north bank of Yangtze River,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:14.05,0:14:18.38,Thinking,Narrator,0,0,0,,leering greedily at the six commanderies of Jiangdong.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:18.38,0:14:21.04,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,Better to ask Sun Quan for Eastern Wu for aid.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:20.60,0:14:24.00,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,400,3000,3400)\pos(959.33,497.893)}Zhūgě Liàng\NStyled: Kǒngmíng
Dialogue: 0,0:14:21.04,0:14:24.06,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,Through an alliance, we can have \Nthe north and south face off,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:24.06,0:14:26.46,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,we would stand to gain amidst that.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:30.38,0:14:32.60,Default,Liu Bei,0,0,0,,Jiangdong has many prodigies.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:33.10,0:14:36.10,Default,Liu Bei,0,0,0,,Would they accept us if they\N have their own ambitions?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:37.37,0:14:38.50,Default,Soldier,0,0,0,,My lord!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:39.74,0:14:40.62,Default,Soldier,0,0,0,,My lord.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:40.62,0:14:43.44,Default,Soldier,0,0,0,,Lu Su, sent by Sun Quan of Wu to offer \Ncondolences, has disembarked here!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:47.88,0:14:50.26,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,When Sun Ce died,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:50.68,0:14:53.66,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,did Xiangyang send someone to express condolences?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:53.68,0:14:56.76,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(325.368,508.178)}Liú Qí
Dialogue: 0,0:14:54.12,0:14:56.76,Default,Liu Qi,0,0,0,,Jiangdong despises us over our killing of Sun Jian!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:56.76,0:14:59.42,Default,Liu Qi,0,0,0,,Why would they come here to spare their pity?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:00.30,0:15:07.60,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,It would appear that Lu Su came to investigate\N our strength under the pretext of mourning.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:09.34,0:15:11.92,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,Cao Cao leads a host of million men.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:11.92,0:15:14.82,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,He has devoured Jianghan and now covets Jiangdong.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:14.82,0:15:17.34,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,Sun Quan cherishes what his family has built,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:17.34,0:15:20.70,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,so he sent someone to explore our position,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:20.70,0:15:23.20,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,implicitly inviting us to join forces.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:24.96,0:15:27.10,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,We are blessed that Lu Su is his envoy!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:27.10,0:15:29.96,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,I say we make use of the wind and sail to Jiangdong!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:30.46,0:15:33.12,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,With my unblemished tongue,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:33.12,0:15:36.93,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,I will incite the North and South into war.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:37.50,0:15:39.14,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,If the southern army wins,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:39.14,0:15:42.37,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,we will pursue Cao Cao and retake Jing Province.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:42.86,0:15:45.10,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,If the northern army wins,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:45.10,0:15:48.12,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,the chaos will present us a chance to take Jiangnan.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:55.40,0:15:57.48,Default,Liu Bei,0,0,0,,That is a strong plan!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:58.70,0:16:01.22,Default,Lu Su,0,0,0,,Sir Kongming, we are approaching Chaisang.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:01.72,0:16:05.00,Default,Lu Su,0,0,0,,For the good of our common cause, I ask for a favor.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:09.10,0:16:11.24,Default,Lu Su,0,0,0,,When you meet with my lord,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:12.52,0:16:13.92,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(969.787,482.956)}Lǔ Sù\NStyled: Zǐjìng
Dialogue: 0,0:16:11.24,0:16:13.92,Default,Lu Su,0,0,0,,do not expose the magnitude of Cao Cao's army.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:17.26,0:16:19.06,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,No need to remind me, Zijing.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:19.06,0:16:21.46,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,I will have my own way of replying.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:25.61,0:16:27.68,Default,Officials,0,0,0,,After you!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:30.16,0:16:31.35,Default,Officials,0,0,0,,My lord!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:31.76,0:16:33.19,Default,Soldier,0,0,0,,Report!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:37.09,0:16:39.50,Default,Soldier,0,0,0,,My lord, Master Lu Su returned from Jiangxia!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:39.50,0:16:40.80,Default,Soldier,0,0,0,,He awaits to be met!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:42.57,0:16:43.50,Default,Sun Quan,0,0,0,,Let him in.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:43.50,0:16:44.38,Default,Soldier,0,0,0,,Yes!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.38,0:16:45.66,Default,Soldier,0,0,0,,We invite Master Lu!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:51.81,0:16:53.47,Default,Lu Su,0,0,0,,My respects, my liege!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:56.35,0:16:58.08,Default,Sun Quan,0,0,0,,Your arrival is welcome!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:58.08,0:17:00.38,Default,Sun Quan,0,0,0,,Cao Mengde just sent an envoy with this letter.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:00.38,0:17:01.74,Default,Sun Quan,0,0,0,,We need to discuss it.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:03.26,0:17:03.80,Default,Sun Quan,0,0,0,,Sit.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:11.68,0:17:16.60,Thinking,Cao Cao,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}Recently, I received orders to subjugate the sinful.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:16.60,0:17:19.56,Thinking,Cao Cao,0,0,0,,{\bord12}My banners pointed southward, \NLiu Cong bound his hands.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:19.56,0:17:22.70,Thinking,Cao Cao,0,0,0,,{\bord12}The people of Jing-Xiang yielded to me upon such a sight!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:23.20,0:17:26.86,Thinking,Cao Cao,0,0,0,,{\bord12}With an army of million men \Nand veteran generals in the thousands,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:26.86,0:17:30.64,Thinking,Cao Cao,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}I will go hunt Liu Bei with you, General, in Jiangxia.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:30.64,0:17:33.64,Thinking,Cao Cao,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}I will share his land with you in goodwill upon victory.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:33.64,0:17:38.50,Thinking,Cao Cao,0,0,0,,{\bord12}Sir must not be a bystander, for I need your quick reply. - Mengde
Dialogue: 0,0:17:41.27,0:17:42.96,Default,Lu Su,0,0,0,,What have you decided upon, my lord?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:42.96,0:17:46.40,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(834.888,415.05)}Sūn Quán \NStyled: Zhòngmóu
Dialogue: 0,0:17:42.96,0:17:46.40,Default,Sun Quan,0,0,0,,No decisions yet. It is still under our fellow gentlemen's discussion.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:46.72,0:17:49.96,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,400,4000,4420)\pos(990.248,342.543)}Zhāng Zhāo\NStyled: Zǐbù
Dialogue: 0,0:17:46.86,0:17:47.78,Default,Lu Su,0,0,0,,My lord, my lord!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:47.78,0:17:48.96,Default,Zhang Zhao,0,0,0,,My lord!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:49.32,0:17:52.28,Default,Zhang Zhao,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}Cao Cao has an army of a million on his side,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:52.28,0:17:55.65,Default,Zhang Zhao,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}pacifying lands by the imperial authority.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:55.65,0:18:01.50,Default,Zhang Zhao,0,0,0,,{\bord12}If we are to resist, only the Yangtze River serves as our bulwark.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:01.50,0:18:04.52,Default,Zhang Zhao,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}But now that Cao Cao has taken Jing Province,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:05.68,0:18:10.48,Default,Zhang Zhao,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}we now share the Yangtze River as our border.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:10.48,0:18:13.76,Default,Zhang Zhao,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}His momentum is unstoppable.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:14.76,0:18:18.30,Default,Zhang Zhao,0,0,0,,{\bord12}Our only option, in my humble opinion,\N is submission.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:18.51,0:18:20.98,Default,Zhang Zhao,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}It is the only way to ensure our survival.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:22.66,0:18:24.39,Default,Officials,0,0,0,,My lord, my lord!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:24.70,0:18:28.28,Default,Officials,0,0,0,,Zibu's words accord with the will of the Heavens!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:33.88,0:18:36.94,Default,Zhang Zhao,0,0,0,,Please have no doubts, my liege.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:36.94,0:18:40.42,Default,Zhang Zhao,0,0,0,,If we surrender, the common people of Wu,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:40.42,0:18:44.54,Default,Zhang Zhao,0,0,0,,and the six commanderies of Jiangdong can be ensured peace and tranquility!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:44.54,0:18:46.98,Default,Officials,0,0,0,,Indeed, my liege!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:52.87,0:18:57.68,Default,Sun Quan,0,0,0,,Who knew that the autumn night\N of Jiangnan would make people shiver so.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:04.04,0:19:06.10,Default,Officials,0,0,0,,Submission is self-protection!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:06.10,0:19:06.82,Default,Officials,0,0,0,,Indeed!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:06.82,0:19:09.12,Default,Officials,0,0,0,,Cao Cao has a million troops!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:16.98,0:19:18.56,Default,Sun Quan,0,0,0,,What is your position?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:22.38,0:19:27.63,Default,Lu Su,0,0,0,,The views of the masses will lead \NYour Lordship to make a grave mistake.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:27.63,0:19:31.48,Default,Lu Su,0,0,0,,A common man might submit to Cao, but you, sire, cannot.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:32.08,0:19:32.83,Default,Sun Quan,0,0,0,,Why?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:33.12,0:19:37.54,Default,Lu Su,0,0,0,,{\bord12}If someone such as I submits to Cao Cao, I may keep my position like before.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:37.54,0:19:41.08,Default,Lu Su,0,0,0,,{\bord12}If you, sire, submitted to Cao Cao, you would be made a mere marquis,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:41.08,0:19:45.54,Default,Lu Su,0,0,0,,{\bord12}with no chariots save one, no more horses than a pair, and few followers left.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:45.54,0:19:48.76,Default,Lu Su,0,0,0,,{\bord12}How could you not be but a fleeting shadow in the eyes of the South?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:51.72,0:19:55.30,Default,Lu Su,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}The gentry only seek their own interests.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:55.64,0:19:57.16,Default,Lu Su,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}They are not to be listened to.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:57.58,0:20:00.40,Default,Lu Su,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}Sire must decide on your plan soon.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:02.74,0:20:06.49,Default,Sun Quan,0,0,0,,{\bord12}The words of my ministers have disappointed me greatly.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:08.18,0:20:11.56,Default,Sun Quan,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}Only your plan matches mine, Zijing.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:12.30,0:20:16.36,Default,Sun Quan,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}This must be the Heavens gifting you to me!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:17.22,0:20:18.70,Default,Sun Quan,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}However...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:18.70,0:20:21.80,Default,Sun Quan,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}Cao Cao has attained the former armies of Yuan Shao
Dialogue: 0,0:20:21.80,0:20:23.74,Default,Sun Quan,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}and now the soldiers of Jing.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:23.74,0:20:27.22,Default,Sun Quan,0,0,0,,{\bord12}With such vast strength, I fear he is too powerful to be withstood.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:28.72,0:20:30.42,Default,Lu Su,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}When I arrived to Jiangxia,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:30.42,0:20:34.04,Default,Lu Su,0,0,0,,{\bord12}I asked the brother of Zhuge Jin,\N Zhuge Liang, to come here.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:34.04,0:20:38.36,Default,Lu Su,0,0,0,,{\bord12}You could inquire of him of the true situation of Cao Cao's army.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:39.84,0:20:41.42,Default,Sun Quan,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}Sleeping Dragon is here?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:41.80,0:20:43.62,Default,Lu Su,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}He is at the guesthouse right now.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:46.32,0:20:47.94,Default,Sun Quan,0,0,0,,It is quite late.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:48.42,0:20:51.64,Default,Sun Quan,0,0,0,,Tomorrow, assemble all officers civil and military.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:51.64,0:20:55.54,Default,Sun Quan,0,0,0,,Ask him to meet the gentry of Jiangdong for a debate.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:59.93,0:21:00.70,Default,Lu Su,0,0,0,,My lord.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:05.78,0:21:06.98,Default,Lu Su,0,0,0,,I take my leave.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:09.64,0:21:11.18,Default,Lu Su,0,0,0,,When you meet with my liege,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:11.18,0:21:13.64,Default,Lu Su,0,0,0,,do not reveal the magnitude of Cao Cao's army.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:14.56,0:21:17.53,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,You reminded me many times on the boat yesterday.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:19.25,0:21:20.82,Default,Lu Su,0,0,0,,Sir Kongming, please.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:23.43,0:21:25.95,Default,Official,0,0,0,,Gentlemen, they are here, they are here!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:28.68,0:21:32.40,Default,Lu Su,0,0,0,,Sir Kongming, do not frighten our lord in any way!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:32.40,0:21:33.38,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,Worry not, Zijing,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:33.38,0:21:35.82,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,I will handle the situation without err.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:38.50,0:21:39.18,Default,Lu Su,0,0,0,,Please.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:42.18,0:21:43.70,Default,Lu Su,0,0,0,,Gentlemen,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:44.11,0:21:46.55,Default,Lu Su,0,0,0,,this is Sir Zhuge Kongming.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:48.54,0:21:50.56,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,Gentlemen, I am fortunate to meet you all!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:52.82,0:21:55.26,Default,Lu Su,0,0,0,,This is the Commissioner-General of the Household,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:55.26,0:21:56.78,Default,Lu Su,0,0,0,,Zhang Zhao, Zhang Zibu.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:57.51,0:21:59.33,Default,Zhang Zhao & Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,Greetings.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:00.32,0:22:02.24,Default,Lu Su,0,0,0,,Gu Yong, Gu Yuantan.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:05.06,0:22:06.20,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,Greetings.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:06.20,0:22:08.44,Default,Lu Su,0,0,0,,Yu Fan, Yu Zhongxiang.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:10.60,0:22:12.68,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(332.143,510.143)}Yú Fān\NStyled: Zhòngxiáng
Dialogue: 0,0:22:12.68,0:22:15.92,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(343.714,486.143)}Bù Zhì\NStyled: Zǐshān
Dialogue: 0,0:22:13.86,0:22:15.92,Default,Lu Su,0,0,0,,Bu Zhi, Bu Zishan.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:15.92,0:22:20.20,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(314.705,464.222)}Xuē Zōng\NStyled: Jìngwén
Dialogue: 0,0:22:16.60,0:22:18.79,Default,Lu Su,0,0,0,,Xue Zong, Xue Jingwen.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:20.20,0:22:25.04,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(371.539,513.244)}Lù Jī\NStyled: Gōngjì
Dialogue: 0,0:22:20.48,0:22:22.84,Default,Lu Su,0,0,0,,Lu Ji, Lu Gongji.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:25.04,0:22:28.60,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(365.5,464.356)}Yán Jùn\NStyled: Màncái
Dialogue: 0,0:22:25.62,0:22:27.56,Default,Lu Su,0,0,0,,Yan Jun, Yan Mancai.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:28.92,0:22:31.88,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,400,2580,2980)\pos(644.078,478.956)}Chéng Bǐng\NStyled: Déshū
Dialogue: 0,0:22:29.29,0:22:31.40,Default,Lu Su,0,0,0,,Cheng Bing, Cheng Deshu.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:33.31,0:22:35.24,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,A pleasure! A pleasure!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:36.55,0:22:38.84,Default,Officials,0,0,0,,Please.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:23.50,0:23:25.37,Default,Zhang Zhao,0,0,0,,Sir Kongming.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:28.97,0:23:32.04,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,Sir Zibu, what can you tell me?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:33.22,0:23:37.78,Default,Zhang Zhao,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}I am the most insignificant of our patricians.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:39.32,0:23:42.90,Default,Zhang Zhao,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}I heard that when you lived in your cottage,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:42.90,0:23:46.06,Default,Zhang Zhao,0,0,0,,{\bord12}you once compared yourself \Nwith Guan Zhong and Yue Yi.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:46.06,0:23:49.62,Default,Zhang Zhao,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}Is this true?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:50.62,0:23:51.49,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}Indeed.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:52.50,0:23:57.28,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}'Tis but a simple comparison to describe my life.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:03.44,0:24:07.96,Default,Zhang Zhao,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}I heard Liu of Yu Province visited your cottage thrice.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:07.96,0:24:10.66,Default,Zhang Zhao,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}Being fortunate enough to meet you,
Dialogue: 0,0:24:10.66,0:24:13.64,Default,Zhang Zhao,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}he compared himself to a fish getting water.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:13.94,0:24:18.44,Default,Zhang Zhao,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}He also swore that he would win the lands of Jing-Xiang.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:21.36,0:24:29.48,Default,Zhang Zhao,0,0,0,,{\bord12}Yet now, the entire province willingly submitted to Cao Cao.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:30.50,0:24:35.96,Default,Zhang Zhao,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}Could sir please explain this matter?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:36.05,0:24:39.35,Default,Officials,0,0,0,,Yes, how do you explain that!
Dialogue: 0,0:24:43.60,0:24:45.34,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}In my opinion,
Dialogue: 0,0:24:45.34,0:24:49.60,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}retaking Jing-Xiang is as easy as turning our palms!
Dialogue: 0,0:24:50.82,0:24:54.00,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}My liege, Liu of Yu, is both humane and just.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:54.00,0:24:57.86,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}He refused to stoop to filching the estate of his kin.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:58.76,0:25:01.86,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}But the callow Liu Cong gave it up under evil duress,
Dialogue: 0,0:25:01.86,0:25:04.02,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}thus did Cao Cao wrench it through force.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:04.02,0:25:09.02,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12}My liege, with forces stationed at Jiangxia, has promising prospects.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:10.02,0:25:14.64,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}But the petty folk would not know this.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:19.71,0:25:24.88,Default,Zhang Zhao,0,0,0,,{\bord12}It would seem your words and your actions contradict each other.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:25.64,0:25:28.26,Default,Zhang Zhao,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}Sir compares yourself to Guan and Yue,
Dialogue: 0,0:25:28.26,0:25:32.30,Default,Zhang Zhao,0,0,0,,{\bord12}yet Guan Zhong led his master Duke Huan of Qi to become a hegemon over the lords.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:32.30,0:25:37.96,Default,Zhang Zhao,0,0,0,,{\bord12}Yue Yi subdued over seventy cities \Nof the mighty Qi for the feeble Yan.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:38.16,0:25:42.06,Default,Zhang Zhao,0,0,0,,{\bord12}These two were men of most\Ncommanding and conspicuous talent.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:42.06,0:25:43.04,Default,Officials,0,0,0,,Indeed, indeed!
Dialogue: 0,0:25:43.04,0:25:46.66,Default,Zhang Zhao,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}Before Liu of Yu obtained your services,
Dialogue: 0,0:25:46.66,0:25:51.00,Default,Zhang Zhao,0,0,0,,{\bord12}he marched free across the land \Na mighty force, seizing cities wherever he went.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:51.52,0:25:56.48,Default,Zhang Zhao,0,0,0,,{\bord12}However, after you \Ncommitted yourself to Lord Liu,
Dialogue: 0,0:25:56.48,0:26:02.45,Default,Zhang Zhao,0,0,0,,{\bord12}his men would drop their arms and armor, fleeing like rats before Cao Cao!
Dialogue: 0,0:26:04.80,0:26:06.98,Default,Zhang Zhao,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}He abandoned Xinye, fled Fancheng,
Dialogue: 0,0:26:06.98,0:26:09.66,Default,Zhang Zhao,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}lost at Dangyang, and now holes up in Xiakou!
Dialogue: 0,0:26:09.66,0:26:12.80,Default,Zhang Zhao,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}Not a single place has been safe enough for him!
Dialogue: 0,0:26:12.80,0:26:14.94,Default,Officials,0,0,0,,Yes, yes!
Dialogue: 0,0:26:15.50,0:26:22.20,Default,Zhang Zhao,0,0,0,,{\bord12}It seems, after you join in service to Lord Liu, he fares worse than before!
Dialogue: 0,0:26:25.00,0:26:32.90,Default,Zhang Zhao,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}Is this truly like Guan Zhong and Yue Yi?
Dialogue: 0,0:26:35.46,0:26:41.61,Default,Zhang Zhao,0,0,0,,{\bord12}Those are my ignoble and blunt thoughts. \NI trust that you will not take offense to it, good sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:50.54,0:26:55.32,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}Can a sparrow ever grasp the aspirations of a swan?
Dialogue: 0,0:26:59.72,0:27:02.68,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}In my time as a humble tiller in Longzhong,
Dialogue: 0,0:27:02.68,0:27:05.76,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}whenever I met a sick person on the verge of death,
Dialogue: 0,0:27:06.48,0:27:10.32,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}I always told the family to first serve them congee,
Dialogue: 0,0:27:11.32,0:27:13.70,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}then administer them mild tonics.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:14.20,0:27:16.13,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}Restoring balance to their organs,
Dialogue: 0,0:27:16.13,0:27:18.76,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}the body will recover slowly but surely.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:19.54,0:27:23.10,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12}Only then could meats \Nand potent drugs be used to cure.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:23.10,0:27:25.90,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}Thus, the root of the disease can be eradicated!
Dialogue: 0,0:27:28.30,0:27:31.68,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12}If it were otherwise, if you do not wait for balance to be restored,
Dialogue: 0,0:27:31.68,0:27:34.22,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}and administering volatile drugs too early,
Dialogue: 0,0:27:34.22,0:27:38.14,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12}recovery will become an arduous task.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:39.46,0:27:43.68,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12}When Imperial Uncle Liu suffered defeat at Runan, he took refuge with Liu Biao.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:44.00,0:27:48.32,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12}He only had less than a thousand men\Nand Generals Guan, Zhang, and Zhao Yun.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:48.32,0:27:51.28,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}He was verily like a man wasted by disease.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:52.90,0:27:56.60,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12}Xinye is a mere small county with few people, \Nscant grain, and weak foundations,
Dialogue: 0,0:27:56.60,0:28:00.58,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12}along with such insufficient forces, with weak and flimsy walls.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:00.58,0:28:04.72,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12}Untrained soldiers, and supplies that can last only a few months.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:05.17,0:28:09.76,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12}Despite this, the fire of Bowang Slope and the flooding of Bai River
Dialogue: 0,0:28:09.76,0:28:14.50,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12}put the enemy commanders, Xiahou Dun and Cao Ren, {\bord12}in a state of panic and disarray!
Dialogue: 0,0:28:15.78,0:28:21.36,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12}I reckon that Guan Zhong and Yue Yi may not surpass such leadership.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:24.98,0:28:27.30,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}As for the loss at Dangyang,
Dialogue: 0,0:28:27.30,0:28:30.82,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12}we had thousands upon thousands\N of people, young and elderly, with us.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:30.82,0:28:32.98,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}Imperial Uncle Liu refused to abandon them.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:32.98,0:28:36.78,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12}Thus, though the march was slow, he never once thought of taking Jiangling,
Dialogue: 0,0:28:36.78,0:28:38.70,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}but willing to suffer with his people!
Dialogue: 0,0:28:38.70,0:28:41.68,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}That is what humanity and righteousness is!
Dialogue: 0,0:28:43.54,0:28:45.06,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}The few cannot oppose the many,
Dialogue: 0,0:28:45.06,0:28:48.36,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}victory and defeat are but common in warfare.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:48.36,0:28:51.44,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12}Emperor Gaozu of Han \Nsuffered many defeats by Xiang Yu,
Dialogue: 0,0:28:51.44,0:28:54.42,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}but had his decisive victory at Gaixia!
Dialogue: 0,0:28:55.39,0:28:57.90,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}Was that not because of the genius of Han Xin?
Dialogue: 0,0:28:59.36,0:29:03.20,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12}Indeed, the strength of a nation, its spirit and well-being...
Dialogue: 0,0:29:03.20,0:29:05.16,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}All must depend on those with grand strategy!
Dialogue: 0,0:29:05.70,0:29:11.02,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12}Not bluffing braggarts or rhetoricians of nonsense.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:11.02,0:29:14.44,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}Those with hollow fame who defraud men,
Dialogue: 0,0:29:14.44,0:29:17.62,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12} sit in complacency and believing themselves above all else,
Dialogue: 0,0:29:17.62,0:29:21.46,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12}yet when faced with danger, \Nprove unable to act!
Dialogue: 0,0:29:23.20,0:29:27.98,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}Truly, a farce for all the world to see and mock!
Dialogue: 0,0:29:33.03,0:29:38.11,Default,Yu Fan,0,0,0,,Chancellor Cao has gathered an army of a million, casting his glare at Jiangxia like a tiger!
Dialogue: 0,0:29:38.65,0:29:44.06,Default,Yu Fan,0,0,0,,I would ask you, sir, of your views on this uncertain future.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:48.78,0:29:54.02,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,Cao Cao has but surrendered rebels and mobs of low morale from Yuan Shao and Liu Biao.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:54.02,0:29:56.64,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,A million they may be, but I fear them not!
Dialogue: 0,0:29:57.46,0:30:01.63,Default,Yu Fan,0,0,0,,But you were defeated at Dangyang and fled to Xiakou in desperation.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:01.63,0:30:06.00,Default,Yu Fan,0,0,0,,In a rout of utter panic, you could hardly find a safe place!
Dialogue: 0,0:30:06.00,0:30:09.96,Default,Yu Fan,0,0,0,,Now you have crossed the river to ask for our help,
Dialogue: 0,0:30:09.96,0:30:11.90,Default,Yu Fan,0,0,0,,and yet say you fear them not.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:12.74,0:30:15.42,Default,Yu Fan,0,0,0,,Truly an arrogant jest!
Dialogue: 0,0:30:18.88,0:30:21.70,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,Are you not Yu Fan, Yu Zhongxiang?
Dialogue: 0,0:30:23.55,0:30:25.32,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,You laugh too early!
Dialogue: 0,0:30:27.32,0:30:33.58,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,Can Imperial Uncle with a few thousand honorable troops win against a million murderous brutes?
Dialogue: 0,0:30:34.50,0:30:37.35,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,Yet still our army is united in defiance!
Dialogue: 0,0:30:37.35,0:30:40.48,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,Regardless of defeat, we will fight to the last!
Dialogue: 0,0:30:41.60,0:30:45.50,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,Jiangdong has elite troops and ample food, with Yangtze as its bastion,
Dialogue: 0,0:30:45.50,0:30:48.74,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,yet still many beg their lord to kneel in submission,
Dialogue: 0,0:30:48.74,0:30:51.00,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,caring not of becoming a mockery of the realm!
Dialogue: 0,0:30:51.21,0:30:56.24,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,As such, Lord Liu of Yu is proud to stand up against the despot Cao!
Dialogue: 0,0:31:01.85,0:31:05.36,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,Back then, you were under the tent of Adminstrator Wang Lang of Kuaiji.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:05.78,0:31:08.20,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,You persuaded him to surrender to Sun Ce.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:09.10,0:31:14.66,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,Who ever expected that under Sun Quan, you would want him to surrender to Cao Cao in return!
Dialogue: 0,0:31:15.18,0:31:19.16,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,Seems like old habits will not die!
Dialogue: 0,0:31:19.45,0:31:23.36,Default,Bu Zhi,0,0,0,,Kongming, is that not going too far?!
Dialogue: 0,0:31:24.19,0:31:27.76,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,Brother Zishan. My apologies.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:31.82,0:31:41.38,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,Note: Sū Qín and Zhāng Yí were rival political strategists of the Warring States period. \NSu Qin led the Vertical Alliance of Six States against Qin, while Zhang Yi led Qin to dissolve it.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:31.72,0:31:36.56,Default,Bu Zhi,0,0,0,,Do you intend to model after Su Qin and Zhang Yi?
Dialogue: 0,0:31:37.36,0:31:41.32,Default,Bu Zhi,0,0,0,,Have you come to win us over with elegant words?
Dialogue: 0,0:31:43.62,0:31:48.88,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12}Does Brother Zishan regard Su Qin and Zhang Yi as mere lobbyists?
Dialogue: 0,0:31:49.40,0:31:52.80,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12}Do you not recognize them \Nas true champions of their time!
Dialogue: 0,0:31:53.40,0:31:56.02,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}Su Qin held the seals of chancellorship of six nations,
Dialogue: 0,0:31:56.02,0:31:58.88,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}Zhang Yi was twice the chancellor of Qin!
Dialogue: 0,0:31:58.88,0:32:02.42,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}Both brought about reformation of their nations!
Dialogue: 0,0:32:02.42,0:32:06.50,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12)}Not like those who cower before \Nthe strong and victimize the weak.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:06.50,0:32:11.88,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12}You gentlemen have never seen a single soldier of Cao, yet urge surrender with craven dispatch.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:11.88,0:32:15.35,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12}Are you the ones to ridicule \NSu Qin and Zhang Yi?
Dialogue: 0,0:32:15.35,0:32:21.20,Default,Xue Zong,0,0,0,,{\bord12}May I ask, sir Kongming, \Nwhat is your view on Cao Cao?
Dialogue: 0,0:32:21.20,0:32:24.02,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}A traitor to the Han! What else is there?
Dialogue: 0,0:32:24.29,0:32:25.49,Default,Xue Zong,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}Sir is mistaken.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:25.82,0:32:29.02,Default,Xue Zong,0,0,0,,{\bord12}The time of the House of Hàn under Heaven is near its end.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:29.02,0:32:34.28,Default,Xue Zong,0,0,0,,{\bord12}Now Cao Cao holds two-thirds of \Nthe empire, the people submit to him!
Dialogue: 0,0:32:34.28,0:32:37.10,Default,Xue Zong,0,0,0,,{\bord12}Liu Xuande refuses to recognize\N the season of history.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:37.10,0:32:40.76,Default,Xue Zong,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}Throwing eggs at rocks, how could he not fail?
Dialogue: 0,0:32:41.74,0:32:42.76,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,Xue Jingwen!
Dialogue: 0,0:32:43.84,0:32:46.36,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,Do you mean to deny both father and lord?!
Dialogue: 0,0:32:46.70,0:32:47.06,Default,Xue Zong,0,0,0,,You-!
Dialogue: 0,0:32:48.98,0:32:53.84,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,To live between Heaven and Earth, loyalty and filiality is the foundation of being!
Dialogue: 0,0:32:54.24,0:32:57.12,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,The Cao clan served the Han Empire and relished its bounty,
Dialogue: 0,0:32:57.12,0:33:00.04,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,yet their ingrate spawn think only of usurpation!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:00.04,0:33:01.96,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,What is he then if not a traitor?!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:02.76,0:33:08.02,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,For these traitors, only suppression \Nand execution by the realm is most fit!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:09.16,0:33:13.68,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,Yet you sir, as an official of the Han,\N commend this despot!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:13.68,0:33:16.24,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,Is that not to deny loyalty and filiality!?
Dialogue: 0,0:33:16.36,0:33:17.08,Default,Xue Zong,0,0,0,,You-!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:18.46,0:33:21.66,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,You are not worthy of discourse! \NUnfit to speak with any further!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:26.38,0:33:30.42,Default,Lu Ji,0,0,0,,Cao Cao may be ruling the lords\N by coercing the Emperor,
Dialogue: 0,0:33:30.42,0:33:33.12,Default,Lu Ji,0,0,0,,but he is still the descendant of Premier Cao Shen.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:30.42,0:33:33.12,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,Note: Cao Shen (曹参) was an early chancellor of the Han, \Naiding Liu Bang in its founding.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:34.80,0:33:41.42,Default,Lu Ji,0,0,0,,Liu Xuande claims to be Prince Jing \Nof Zhongshan's descendant, yet no evidence exists.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:41.42,0:33:45.58,Default,Lu Ji,0,0,0,,We know that he is but a\N weaver of mats and seller of shoes!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:46.40,0:33:48.76,Default,Lu Ji,0,0,0,,How is he worthy enough to challenge Cao Cao?
Dialogue: 0,0:34:10.48,0:34:11.44,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,Master Lu?
Dialogue: 0,0:34:12.50,0:34:14.78,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,Is that gentleman not...
Dialogue: 0,0:34:15.44,0:34:19.66,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,The Young Lu who stole oranges\N from Yuan Shu in front of guests?
Dialogue: 0,0:34:20.58,0:34:22.08,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,Lu Gongji?
Dialogue: 0,0:34:27.40,0:34:30.10,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,Please sit down. Heed just a word from me.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:31.32,0:34:36.42,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,Cao Cao is indeed a descendant of Premier Cao, thus he is to be a consul of the Han!
Dialogue: 0,0:34:37.60,0:34:41.50,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,Yet now, Cao Cao domineers and abuses his power, and abuses his sovereign.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:41.50,0:34:44.98,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,He shames not just the Emperor, he shames his ancestors as well!
Dialogue: 0,0:34:44.98,0:34:48.77,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,Not only is he a rebel consul of Han, he is also a traitor of his clan!
Dialogue: 0,0:34:49.94,0:34:53.29,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,Imperial Uncle Liu is an imperial scion of dignity.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:53.29,0:34:56.10,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,The Emperor inspected the clan registry to confer nobility,
Dialogue: 0,0:34:56.10,0:34:58.60,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,even naming him the "Imperial Uncle."
Dialogue: 0,0:34:59.58,0:35:02.08,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,Can you say no evidence exists now?
Dialogue: 0,0:35:03.94,0:35:07.28,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,Gaozu began as a village corporal and ended as the emperor.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:07.28,0:35:10.90,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,So what shame is there in\N weaving mats and selling shoes?
Dialogue: 0,0:35:10.90,0:35:14.76,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,Sir, your puerile views are unfit for an eminent scholar.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:14.88,0:35:15.74,Default,Lu Ji,0,0,0,,You-!
Dialogue: 0,0:35:19.50,0:35:24.68,Default,Yan Jun,0,0,0,,Kongming, all that you have said is but bombast, not reason.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:25.25,0:35:28.68,Default,Yan Jun,0,0,0,,Gentlemen, there is no need to argue with him.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:29.72,0:35:32.22,Default,Yan Jun,0,0,0,,Let me pose this question, Kongming.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:32.48,0:35:34.42,Default,Yan Jun,0,0,0,,What canons have you studied?
Dialogue: 0,0:35:38.46,0:35:42.74,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12}I am no student of grabbing lines from chapters or singling phrases from canons.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:43.48,0:35:46.84,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}That is the passion of geriatrics and pedants.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:46.84,0:35:49.76,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}It has no use for building a nation or governance.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:52.05,0:35:57.32,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12}Of the wise sages since antiquity, \Nnot all of them mastered the canons.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:58.50,0:36:00.50,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}The Chancellor of King Tang of Shang, Yi Yin,
Dialogue: 0,0:36:00.50,0:36:04.08,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12}began as nothing more than \Na slave who tilled fields.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:04.08,0:36:08.96,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12}Jiang Ziya, who built the Zhou, once cast his hooks into the Wei River to fish.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:09.84,0:36:15.50,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,Note Chen Ping (陳平) was another early chancellor of the Han\N who helped Liu Bang maintain stability after unification.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:09.84,0:36:15.50,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12}Zhang Liang and Chen Ping of later ages, were all men of transcendent ability.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:16.60,0:36:19.72,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}I never heard what canons they mastered!
Dialogue: 0,0:36:20.03,0:36:20.47,Default,Yan Jun,0,0,0,,That...!
Dialogue: 0,0:36:21.84,0:36:26.72,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12}A pity the scholars of today repeat only ancient classics and parrot old adages,
Dialogue: 0,0:36:26.72,0:36:29.32,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}wasting their days on brush and inkstone!
Dialogue: 0,0:36:29.32,0:36:35.40,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12}I think these men can only bicker over petty matters behind the back flourishing words and wasting ink!
Dialogue: 0,0:36:35.40,0:36:38.34,Default,Cheng Bing,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}You, sir, are certainly given to exaggeration.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:39.02,0:36:41.74,Default,Cheng Bing,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}But you have not shown any true learning yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:42.02,0:36:46.40,Default,Cheng Bing,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}I pity that you will be ridiculed by scholars!
Dialogue: 0,0:36:49.11,0:36:51.04,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}Then if we must talk about scholars,
Dialogue: 0,0:36:51.48,0:36:55.40,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12}then you must know the scholars' discernment of noble and lesser men?
Dialogue: 0,0:36:55.44,0:37:00.12,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12}A noble scholar is devoted to the nation, compassionate and just, standing against evil.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:00.12,0:37:04.00,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12}If appraised in the present, \Nhis name lives on in the future.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:04.00,0:37:06.06,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}But not so with lesser men!
Dialogue: 0,0:37:06.06,0:37:10.22,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12}Slaving over paper and ink, able only to produce trifles and trickery.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:10.22,0:37:13.50,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12}Writing odes in callow youth, devoted to the canons in old age,
Dialogue: 0,0:37:13.50,0:37:17.60,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12}from his brush flows a thousand words, yet not one thought housed within him.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:18.98,0:37:23.70,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,Note: Yang Xiong (揚雄) (53 BCE–18 CE) was a Ruist philosopher and writer of the late Western Han.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:18.98,0:37:23.70,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12}Look at Yang Xiong! He glorified the age with his writing, his thoughts and poetry.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:23.70,0:37:27.82,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,Note: Wang Mang [王莽], a traditionalist minister turned usurper of the Western Han dynasty.\N His reactionary reforms led to the eventual decline and fall of his reign.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:23.70,0:37:27.82,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12}Yet when vile Wang Mang usurped the throne, he stooped to serve him without shame.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:27.82,0:37:30.80,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12}Thus, his end was met \Nby throwing himself off a tower!
Dialogue: 0,0:37:31.20,0:37:33.26,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}These are the lesser pedants!
Dialogue: 0,0:37:33.26,0:37:37.32,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12}They may draft ten thousand words,\N yet none with value to speak of!
Dialogue: 0,0:37:37.37,0:37:38.09,Default,Cheng Bing,0,0,0,,You...!
Dialogue: 0,0:37:39.82,0:37:43.14,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}Deshu, I respect you as a great scholar of Runan.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:43.68,0:37:49.98,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,Note: "Selections from the Book of Changes"{\i0} (周易摘) is a real book written by Cheng Bing in history, along with two other major works
Dialogue: 0,0:37:43.58,0:37:47.22,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12}I have read your great {\i1}Selections from the Book of Changes{\i0} as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:47.22,0:37:51.90,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12}I wish you could be a noble scholar, who honors the nation.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:52.50,0:37:55.88,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}Not to imitate lesser men such as Yang Xiong,
Dialogue: 0,0:37:56.00,0:37:59.44,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,{\bord12}and leave your name cursed by posterity for days to come.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:59.44,0:38:00.62,Default,Cheng Bing,0,0,0,,Kongming-!
Dialogue: 0,0:38:00.93,0:38:02.20,Default,Cheng Bing,0,0,0,,How dare you!
Dialogue: 0,0:38:02.32,0:38:04.61,Default,Huang Gai,0,0,0,,Cease this infernal squabble!
Dialogue: 0,0:38:08.18,0:38:11.22,Default,Huang Gai,0,0,0,,Sir Kongming is a genius of our generation!
Dialogue: 0,0:38:11.22,0:38:15.18,Default,Huang Gai,0,0,0,,Yet you besmirch him with barbs, breaching the etiquette of hospitality.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:12.72,0:38:17.44,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,400,4300,4720)\pos(971.665,494.596)}Huáng Gài \NStyled: Gōngfù
Dialogue: 0,0:38:15.52,0:38:21.02,Default,Huang Gai,0,0,0,,Our foe is before us, yet instead of planning our defense, you whine like toddlers!
Dialogue: 0,0:38:21.02,0:38:22.18,Default,Huang Gai,0,0,0,,Have you no dignity?
Dialogue: 0,0:38:24.06,0:38:24.65,Default,Huang Gai,0,0,0,,Sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:26.19,0:38:27.11,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,General Huang.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:27.11,0:38:30.78,Default,Huang Gai,0,0,0,,Sir, talking may yield profit, but there is more from silence.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:30.78,0:38:32.94,Default,Huang Gai,0,0,0,,What will you gain by debating these cowards?
Dialogue: 0,0:38:32.94,0:38:36.38,Default,Huang Gai,0,0,0,,Better to speak your views directly to my lord.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:36.38,0:38:41.28,Default,Huang Gai,0,0,0,,How to unite our factions to defeat Cao Cao is the pressing issue!
Dialogue: 0,0:38:42.15,0:38:44.20,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,Senior general, you said it quite well.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:44.50,0:38:49.81,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,These folks all rose to ask, so it was my obligation to answer, that is all.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:49.81,0:38:52.33,Default,Huang Gai,0,0,0,,Please follow me to meet my lord!
Dialogue: 0,0:38:52.83,0:38:53.44,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,Good.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:53.94,0:38:54.52,Default,Huang Gai,0,0,0,,Let's go.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:59.25,0:39:00.26,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,Gentlemen?
Dialogue: 0,0:39:00.68,0:39:01.80,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,So sorry!
Dialogue: 0,0:39:04.34,0:39:06.52,Default,Bu Zhi,0,0,0,,That Zhuge Kongming dares talk down to us!
Dialogue: 0,0:39:06.52,0:39:10.46,Default,Zhang Zhao,0,0,0,,If we let him meet our liege, he will ruin us and our Eastern Wu!
Dialogue: 0,0:39:10.46,0:39:11.72,Default,Officials,0,0,0,,Yes!
Dialogue: 0,0:39:36.28,0:39:42.36,Thinking,Song,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}The blade's light and sword's shadow fade,
Dialogue: 0,0:39:42.36,0:39:48.44,Thinking,Song,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}afar is the drum's beat and horn's serenade,
Dialogue: 0,0:39:48.44,0:39:54.52,Thinking,Song,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}Before my eyes appear, one by one,
Dialogue: 0,0:39:54.52,0:40:00.46,Thinking,Song,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}such vibrant visages.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:00.46,0:40:07.00,Thinking,Song,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}The old paths are buried now
Dialogue: 0,0:40:07.00,0:40:13.10,Thinking,Song,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}by a fire burning through every town.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:13.10,0:40:20.00,Thinking,Song,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}But time, you cannot take away that string
Dialogue: 0,0:40:20.00,0:40:25.10,Thinking,Song,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}of still familiar names.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:25.10,0:40:31.42,Thinking,Song,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}What man will determine victory or death?
Dialogue: 0,0:40:31.42,0:40:37.64,Thinking,Song,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}Prosperity and decline have no cause, indeed!
Dialogue: 0,0:40:37.64,0:40:42.50,Thinking,Song,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}A single breeze scatters the clouds
Dialogue: 0,0:40:42.50,0:40:49.82,Thinking,Song,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}and the world as we know it vanishes with them.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:49.82,0:40:56.10,Thinking,Song,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}Meetings and partings happen for their reasons,
Dialogue: 0,0:40:56.10,0:41:02.32,Thinking,Song,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}but these comings and going still rouse our feelings!
Dialogue: 0,0:41:02.32,0:41:08.52,Thinking,Song,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}We carry the weight of our pasts
Dialogue: 0,0:41:08.52,0:41:14.64,Thinking,Song,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}and account little for the opinions left behind.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:14.64,0:41:20.74,Thinking,Song,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}The Long River's soul turns to tears,
Dialogue: 0,0:41:20.74,0:41:26.88,Thinking,Song,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}the Long River's waters rise in a song,
Dialogue: 0,0:41:26.88,0:41:33.10,Thinking,Song,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}In the skies of history there yet shines a few stars,
Dialogue: 0,0:41:33.10,0:41:38.54,Thinking,Song,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}in the world of man there dwells a spirit of heroism,
Dialogue: 0,0:41:38.54,0:41:52.74,Thinking,Song,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,660)}galloping ever forward.
Comment: 0,0:14:13.79,0:14:16.28,Default,Zhuge Liang,0,0,0,,-It would be hard to resist Cao Cao's large host.

